Project Mu: turn off Google services and telemetry by default

Default-value changes only; every setting stays user-adjustable:

  * signin.allowed / signin.allowed_on_next_startup -> false
    (no "Sign in to Chromium" prompts; on desktop the startup pref is
    copied into signin.allowed at every launch, so both are flipped)
  * translate.enabled -> false (no Google Translate offers)
  * net.network_prediction_options -> kDisabled (no preloading/prefetch)
  * user_experience_metrics.reporting_enabled -> false, independent of the
    installer's registry consent

diff --git a/chrome/browser/browser_process_impl.cc b/chrome/browser/browser_process_impl.cc
index bed9453..d266d92 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/browser_process_impl.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/browser_process_impl.cc
@@ -1354,8 +1354,10 @@ void BrowserProcessImpl::RegisterPrefs(PrefRegistrySimple* registry) {
       password_manager::prefs::kPinAuthenticationAvailableOnChromeOS, false);
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
 
+  // Project Mu: metrics and crash reporting are always off by default,
+  // regardless of any installer consent stored in the registry.
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(metrics::prefs::kMetricsReportingEnabled,
-                                GoogleUpdateSettings::GetCollectStatsConsent());
+                                false);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kDevToolsRemoteDebuggingAllowed, true);
   registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kDevToolsRemoteDebuggingEnabled, false);
 
